# Copy to .env and edit. Defaults match the local vLLM server.
# Deployed, the pair names one of the model Apps: `assistant-llm-v2` serves
# `gemma-4-12b-it`, `assistant-llm-qwen` serves `qwen3.8-27b`,
# `assistant-llm-qwen-int4` serves `qwen3.8-27b-int4`; the endpoint is the
# App's .modal.run URL plus /v1 (docs/OPERATIONS_MAP.md).
# Model sets. `MODEL=comet` reads `MODEL_COMET_*` (and
# `AGENT_COMET_CONTEXT_TOKENS` for the budget) instead of the plain `MODEL_*`
# lines below; every set is published with the secret, so switching is this
# one line and a control-plane redeploy, and no key overwrites another.
# MODEL=
# MODEL_COMET_ENDPOINT=https://api.cometapi.com/v1
# MODEL_COMET_NAME=glm-5.3-flash
# MODEL_COMET_API_KEY=
# MODEL_COMET_AUTH_STYLE=bearer
# MODEL_COMET_EXTRA_BODY={"tool_stream": true}
# AGENT_COMET_CONTEXT_TOKENS=131072
MODEL_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
MODEL_NAME=gemma-4-12b-it
# MODEL_API_KEY=
# MODEL_AUTH_STYLE=bearer
# For a protected Modal `.modal.run` endpoint, use a `wk-....ws-...` proxy
# token above and set MODEL_AUTH_STYLE=modal_proxy.
# The wait for a request's first byte. 600, because a deployed endpoint
# creating a snapshot answers after six or seven minutes and a client that
# asks again only queues a second copy.
# MODEL_TIMEOUT=600
# Output cap only. The server's own context ceiling is separate and is read from
# it, not set here; on the deployed endpoint it is 64k since 2026-08-30.
# MODEL_MAX_TOKENS=8192
# MODEL_TEMPERATURE=0
# Extra attempts after the first, for a server that is busy or still starting.
# MODEL_RETRIES=2
# MODEL_RETRY_BACKOFF=0.5
# Sent to the server's chat template on every request, as JSON. For the Qwen
# Apps this is the thinking dial: the server default is off, and
# {"enable_thinking": true, "reasoning_effort": "low"} turns it on without a
# boot of the model App (publish the secret, redeploy the control plane).
# MODEL_CHAT_TEMPLATE_KWARGS=
# Fields merged into every request body, last, as JSON: what a hosted service
# wants and the OpenAI shape has no word for. GLM through CometAPI:
# {"tool_stream": true}; DeepSeek: {"thinking": {"type": "disabled"}}.
# MODEL_EXTRA_BODY=

# The agent's own settings.
AGENT_DATABASE=data/memory.sqlite3
# Deployed profile only: pooled PostgreSQL DSN, including TLS options. Keep it
# in a platform secret, never in this file or Git.
# AGENT_DATABASE_URL=
# AGENT_DATABASE_SCHEMA=public
# Turns still in flight, in LangGraph's schema. Safe to delete.
AGENT_CHECKPOINTS=data/checkpoints.sqlite3
# The only directory the filesystem tools may read and write. Created if absent.
AGENT_WORKSPACE=workspace
# AGENT_KEEP_TURNS=2
# AGENT_SUMMARIZE_AFTER=16
# AGENT_RETRIEVED_FACTS=5
# The share of the model's own context length one request may occupy. The
# length itself is read from the server, so raising vLLM's --max-model-len is
# all it takes to give the agent more room.
# AGENT_CONTEXT_FRACTION=0.8
# A budget in tokens instead of that share, when you want to name one. Always
# clamped to what the server reports it accepts, so this can only ever ask for
# less than the model allows, never more than it can serve. Unset means the
# fraction decides. It belongs to one agent, and an agent belongs to one person.
# AGENT_CONTEXT_TOKENS=32768
# A hosted service that reports no context length leaves the fraction with
# nothing to take a share of; name a budget here for such a model, or every
# call carries the whole thread and is paid for by the token.
# What one turn may spend before it stops and says so. These are the only
# ceiling on an autonomous turn: the loop ends when the model stops asking for
# tools, and nothing else limits how long it may keep asking. A crossed limit
# is not an error — no further tool runs and the model is asked once more,
# without tools, for the answer you are owed.
# AGENT_TURN_MAX_STEPS=12
# AGENT_TURN_MAX_TOOL_CALLS=24
# AGENT_TURN_MAX_SECONDS=300
# Record what each turn cost and where its time went. On by default, because a
# turn nobody measured is a turn nobody can improve. Timings, counts and
# technical metadata only — never message text, prompts or tool results — and it
# can never fail a turn. The deployed profile uses AGENT_DATABASE_URL instead of
# the file below.
# AGENT_TELEMETRY=true
# AGENT_TELEMETRY_DATABASE=data/telemetry.sqlite3
# Show the answer as it is written instead of when it is finished. Only finished
# messages are stored either way.
# AGENT_STREAM_ANSWERS=true

# Telegram adapter. TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS is a comma-separated list of numeric
# Telegram user ids; an empty list means nobody may use the bot.
TELEGRAM_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS=
# Admit every Telegram account instead of the list above. Deliberate, never a default.
TELEGRAM_OPEN_ACCESS=false

# The web. Three capabilities, configured separately because they cost
# differently. Search asks a provider and spends its credit; fetching spends
# nothing; viewing runs a browser over someone else's JavaScript.
# Empty means the assistant has no search tool at all, rather than one that fails.
WEB_FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=
# WEB_FIRECRAWL_ENDPOINT=https://api.firecrawl.dev/v1
# WEB_SEARCH_RESULTS=5
# Direct fetch. The byte cap bounds what one page may take of the context.
# WEB_FETCH_TIMEOUT=20
# WEB_MAX_REDIRECTS=3
# WEB_MAX_BYTES=1000000
# Most sites answer an unknown client with a challenge page, so the default
# agent string is browser-shaped. A few — Wikimedia measurably — refuse that and
# ask for a client that names itself and a contact. Set this to
# `name/version (your contact)` and those pages become readable; it is empty by
# default because inventing a contact address for you would be worse.
# WEB_FALLBACK_USER_AGENT=
# Viewing. May this process open a web page in its own browser? True on a
# personal machine. The deployed agent image sets it to 0, so a container
# holding the bot token and the database URL refuses instead of quietly
# rendering when no isolated renderer is configured.
# WEB_LOCAL_BROWSER=true
# The isolated, secretless renderer function and its proxy token pair. Required
# in the deployed profile.
#
# The address is deliberately named DEPLOY_ prefixed here: it decides *where* a
# page is opened, and a copy under its own name would send every local
# view_web_page to the deployed renderer, starting a container to do what the
# browser on this machine does for free. tools/sync_control_secret.py publishes
# it to the deployment as WEB_RENDERER_URL.
# DEPLOY_WEB_RENDERER_URL=
# WEB_RENDERER_KEY=
